# CacheLayer

Silent Cursor hooks call CacheLayer before and after allowlisted tools. Do not call `lookup_step` or `save_step` before every native tool.

## Keep stable

Keep this rule short and unchanged across turns so the editor can reuse the same instruction block.

## When compacting

Preserve active file paths, open tasks, decisions still in force, and errors being fixed. Drop large file dumps and repeated tool outputs.

## When to use MCP tools

- Resuming a run: `run_status(run_id)`
- Explicit reuse of an expensive step the hooks may have missed
- Before a risky write: `check_conflict(intended_action, run_id)` if you want an extra guard

## Do not

- Call `lookup_step` before every `Read` / `Shell` / `Grep`
- Call CacheLayer tools before other CacheLayer tools
- Save secrets from env files
